# p4pilot — sample Helix change-submit trigger notes (submit deny for bot user)
#
# PURPOSE
#   Optional second layer on top of protections: a change-submit (or similar)
#   trigger that rejects submit when the submitting user is the agent bot.
#
# SAFETY
#   - Templates and documentation only.
#   - Do not install on production without admin review and a sandbox rehearsal.
#   - Companion scripts refuse to run unless P4PILOT_ALLOW_TRIGGER_INSTALL=1
#     (and still only print guidance — they do not call p4 triggers by default).
#
# ILLUSTRATIVE NAMES
#   Bot user: p4pilot-agent
#   Trigger name: p4pilot-deny-agent-submit
#   Script path placeholders: use paths on YOUR trigger host, not these samples.

# =============================================================================
# Example triggers table fragment (COMMENTED — adapt before use)
# =============================================================================
#
# Form (conceptual; confirm with `p4 help triggers` for your version):
#
#   p4pilot-deny-agent-submit change-submit //... "/path/to/check-submit-deny.sh %user% %change% %client%"
#
# Windows trigger host example (paths and quoting are site-specific):
#
#   p4pilot-deny-agent-submit change-submit //... "powershell.exe -NoProfile -File C:\p4\triggers\check-submit-deny.ps1 -User %user% -Change %change% -Client %client%"
#
# Notes:
#   - Trigger type names and argument substitution tokens differ by version.
#   - Prefer matching on authenticated user identity, not client hostname alone.
#   - Exit non-zero (and print a clear message to stderr) to deny the submit.
#   - Log denials to your studio audit sink if required by policy.
#   - Keep human submitters unaffected: only deny when user == p4pilot-agent
#     (or membership in group ai-agents, if you implement a group lookup).

# =============================================================================
# Behavioral contract for the check script
# =============================================================================
#
# Inputs (typical): submitting user, changelist number, client name
# Decision:
#   if user is p4pilot-agent (or in ai-agents deny-list):
#       print reason → exit 1  (submit denied)
#   else:
#       exit 0                 (submit allowed by this trigger)
#
# This trigger is NOT a replacement for:
#   - removing p4_submit from p4pilot (product boundary)
#   - P4PILOT_POLICY restricted-agent / read-only
#   - sane protections / path limits
#
# See also:
#   check-submit-deny.sh
#   check-submit-deny.ps1
#   ../VERIFY.md
#   ../README.md
